# PMSM V/f Control

**Project Type:** Engineering / Motor Control Project
**Focus:** Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motor Modelling and V/f Control

## Project Overview

This project focused on the **modelling and control of a Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motor (PMSM)** using a Variable Frequency (V/f) control approach. The project explored how the applied voltage and electrical frequency influence the motor's operating speed and overall behaviour.

The work involved developing and analysing the PMSM model, applying the V/f control strategy, and observing the motor's response under different operating conditions. This provided an opportunity to connect theoretical concepts from electrical machines and control systems with practical simulation-based analysis.

## Engineering Skills Developed

* PMSM modelling
* Variable Frequency (V/f) control
* Electrical machine analysis
* Motor speed control
* Understanding voltage and frequency relationships
* Simulation and analysis of motor behaviour
* Control-system fundamentals
* Troubleshooting and interpreting simulation results

## Project Outcome

The project strengthened my understanding of **PMSM operation and motor-control techniques**, particularly the relationship between voltage, frequency and motor speed. It also developed my ability to model an electrical machine and evaluate its behaviour using simulation tools.

